cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ITACA, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "ITACA: Integrated Toolkit for Aerospace Computation and Analysis"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Neves
    given-names: Geovana
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-07-30
# No per-release `doi:` here, deliberately. Zenodo mints the v0.2.0 DOI when
# this tag is archived, so a value written before the tag can only be the
# PREVIOUS release's, which is what shipped in the v0.1.0 record: this file
# carried 10.5281/zenodo.21482649 (the v0.1.0 DOI) beside `version: 0.1.0`
# while the v0.2.0 tag was being prepared, and there is no `.zenodo.json`, so
# Zenodo falls back to this file for deposit metadata. The concept DOI below
# resolves to the latest version and is the one to cite when a specific
# release is not meant.
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21482648
    description: Concept DOI, resolving to the latest version.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21482649
    description: Version DOI for v0.1.0.
repository-code: "https://github.com/nevesgeovana/itaca"
abstract: >-
  Python library for rigorous engineering data management, analysis, and
  computation in aerospace applications: multidimensional datasets with
  mandatory provenance, two-component GUM uncertainty propagation with
  covariance, and origin tags. This release adds the analysis operations,
  the axes and vector-group system with rotation and moment transfer,
  replayable pipelines, and reusable processors defined by an .itceq
  equation file. Publication-quality plotting is roadmapped rather than
  released in this version.
keywords:
  - aerospace
  - wind tunnel
  - uncertainty quantification
  - data management
  - provenance
